\begin{document}

Let $x$ and $y$ be whole numbers such that $1 \leq x, y \leq 10$. My friend picks the numbers $x-4$ and $2y-1$. The product of these numbers is one greater than the product of my numbers:

\begin{align*}
  (2y-1)(x-4) &= xy + 1 \\
  xy &= (2y-1)(x-4) - 1 \\[2ex]
  xy &= (2x-2y-x+4-1) \\
  xy &= (2x-2y-x+5).
\end{align*}

Since $y$ is a whole number, $x=y-2$ is the only integer solution for $x$ in the given range that satisfies the given equation:

\begin{align*}
  xy &= (2x-2y-x+5) \\
  (y-2)(y-3) &= (2y-2(y-2)-(y-2)+5) \\
  \Rightarrow y&=4.
\end{align*}

Now, we can find the product of the numbers I chose for the problem:

\begin{align*}
  xy &= (2y-1)(x-4) \\
  &= (2\cdot4-1)((4-4)+2) \\
  &= 3\cdot2 = \boxed{6}
\end{align*}

\end{document}

