We can solve the determinant step by step using the process of expansion by minors when a row or column contains multiple identical terms.

Expansion by minors will give an expression of the form:

\[A\cdot D_1 + B\cdot D_2 + C\cdot D_3\]

with the sub-determinants:
\begin{align*}
D_1 &= \begin{vmatrix}
\csc^2 x & 1 \\
\cot^2 x & \csc^2 x
\end{vmatrix} = \csc^2 x\cdot \cot^2 x - \csc^4 x, \\
D_2 &= \begin{vmatrix}
. \sec^2 x & 1 \\
1 & \csc^2 x
\end{vmatrix} = . \sec^2 x\cdot \csc^2 x - 1, \\
D_3 &= \begin{vmatrix}
1 & 1 \\
\cos^2 x & \csc^2 x
\end{vmatrix} = \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x.
\end{align*}

Now, let's assign each of the sub-determinants to variables:

\begin{align*}
A &= \sec^2 x, \\
B &= -\sec^2 x + 1, \\
C &= 1 - \cos^2 x.
\end{align*}

