&= 1 + \frac{1}{2} \sum_{n = -864}^{864} \cos(2\pi n / 1729),
\end{align*}
where we have used the periodicity of the cosine function and set $j - k = n.$ Using the geometric series formula for the sum, we find
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = -864}^{864} \cos(2\pi n / 1729) &= \sum_{n = 0}^{1727} \cos(2\pi n / 1729) - \sum_{n = 0}^{863} \cos(2\pi (n + 864) / 1729) \\
&= \sum_{n = 0}^{1727} \cos(2\pi n / 1729) - \sum_{n = 0}^{863} \cos(2\pi \frac{1727-n}{1729}) \\
&= 2 \sum_{n = 0}^{1727} \cos(2\pi n / 1729) - \sum_{n = 0}^{1727} \cos(2\pi n / 1729) \\
&= 0.
\end{align*}
Hence,
