\boxed{\text{(Average of four side lengths)}}

Next, we calculate the semi-perimeter ($s$), which is half of the perimeter we just found:

[asy]
real s = peri_half;
write(Semi-perimeter:\\,s);
[/asy]

\boxed{<semi-perimeter value>}

Now calculate the area:

[asy]
real area = sqrt(s*(s-6)*(s-2)*(s-2)*(s-4));
write(Area:\\, area);
