Next, since all the students are independent, the probability of guessing incorrectly for each of the 4 remaining students is the product of the probabilities of guessing incorrectly for each individual student.

\begin{align*}
p &= \paren{\frac{16}{20}}^{4} \\
&= \paren{\frac{4}{5}}^{4} \\
&= \frac{256}{625}
\end{align*}

However, we want the complementary probability of correctly guessing for each of the 4 students, which is:

\begin{align*}
1 - p &= 1 - \frac{256}{625} \\
&= \frac{369}{625}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the probability of correctly guessing which paper each of the four remaining students is \boxed{\frac{369}{625}}.

