Since probability is a fraction of 1 (between 0 and 1), we can simplify this product by finding a common factor of both numerator and denominator that we can divide by. Here, the common factor is 1. Therefore, the probability is:

\boxed{\dfrac{\left( \dfrac{1}{20}\right)^4}{\left(\dfrac{20}{20}\right)^4}}
\boxed{\dfrac{1}{16000}}

(Fraction does not have units.)

