\frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial A^2} &= 0 \\
\frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial A \partial B} &= 0 \\
\frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial B^2} &= -2
\end{align*}
Since $\frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial B^2} < 0,$ this is indeed a minimum. Thus, the minimum value of the expression is
\boxed{ 2\left(\frac{1}{2}\right) + \frac{1}{\left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)} = \boxed{4 - 2 = \boxed{2}} }

